2.text:
The five exemplars are all CVC with

* 1st  C ∈ {c,d,g,l}
* 2nd  V ∈ {a,o,u}
* 3rd  C ∈ {b,d,t,w}

and in particular the third consonant is never r,p,o,m,e.  That is the
property that separates

dad dab gut low cat

from

ear  cop  ego  mom  ate

on the third position.

On that third-position criterion

* leg  … g  ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* dam  … m  ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* rat  … t  ∈ {b,d,t,w}
* car  … r  ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* bin  … n  ∉ {b,d,t,w}

so that rat is the only item of the five that can be made to satisfy
the exemplar third-letter set.  In the usual sense all of the other four
items are non-examples of the exemplar class, e.g. leg is a very clear
non-example because it introduces the e-vowel which never occurs in the
second position of the exemplars and its third consonant g is not in
{b,d,t,w}.  This is the same reason why dam, car and bin are
non-examples of the dad–dab–gut–low–cat class.

