2.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The five exemplars dad dab gut low cat are monosyllabic CVC with material {a,b,c,d,g,l,o,t,u,w}. In practice C1∈{c,d,g,l}, V∈{a,o,u}, C3∈{b,d,t,w} and crucially {e,m,p,r}∩word=∅. The five quoted non-exemplars ear cop ego mom ate all break the CVC ∧ {e,m,p,r}-free separator, ear/ego/ate by e, cop by p, mom by m, ear by r.

Current round convergence: the separator actually used in the task statement is CVC ∧ {e,m,p,r}∩word=∅, realised in the exemplars as V∈{a,o,u} and C3∈{b,d,t,w}. On that reading:

* leg = l e g contains e, V=e∉{a,o,u}, C3=g∉{b,d,t,w}
* dam = d a m contains m, C3=m∉{b,d,t,w}
* rat = r a t contains r, C1=r∉{c,d,g,l}
* car = c a r contains r, C3=r∉{b,d,t,w}
* bin = b i n is CVC and {e,m,p,r}-free

Hence leg, dam, rat and car are all non-members of the dad/dab/gut/low/cat family, bin is the unique distractor that keeps the {e,m,p,r}-free CVC type.

Disagreement persists on strictness: strict material reading C1 V C3 with C1{c,d,g,l}, V{a,o,u}, C3{b,d,t,w} would also reject bin because i∉V and b∉C1, n∉C3, and rat would be the only option hitting the admissible C3=t. The e,m,p,r-free CVC reading best explains why the five quoted counter-examples are chosen, and it makes bin the conforming odd man out among A-E.

Consensus in round 1: leg is the textbook, most immediately obvious non-follower because it introduces the e-vowel that drives ear/ego/ate and violates the admissible V and C3 sets. Dam, rat and car are non-members for the same e,m,p,r avoidance reason. If a single non-member has to be named, A. leg is the clearest prototypical violation; E. bin is the only option that is actually of the same type as the exemplars under the looser e,m,p,r-free CVC description. Unresolved is whether the vowel set must be strictly {a,o,u} which would also penalise bin’s i, and whether first/third consonant inventories are required versus just e,m,p,r avoidance.

